#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221094 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7095c46-33cf-5407-be83-70a49cf6eadd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a General Update Formula for the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/id #uuid "c3550cab-110a-5344-be19-d183b55bc098" :question/math-academy-id "e-21312" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny' = 2x^2+3xy, \\qquad y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nThe **implicit** Euler method is applied with step size $\\Delta x = 1.$ \nFind the general formula for the new $y$ value, $y_\\text{new},$ in terms of the new value $x_\\text{new}$ and the current value $y.$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y_0 = y(x_0),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = y'_\\text{new} \\cdot \\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwith $y'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new},y_\\text{new})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $\\Delta y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into $y_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y$ and solve for the general formula for $y_\\text{new}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1-3{x}_{\\text{new}}) & =y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{1-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221095 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "246a84b2-e9fa-58e5-858c-66c09e1c3bc0" :knowledge-point/title "Computing One Step Using the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/id #uuid "503c762b-0313-598a-a80c-c53d14ec250a" :question/math-academy-id "e-21318" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny' = x^2y + e^x, \\qquad y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with one step to approximate $y\\left(\\dfrac12\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y_0 = y(x_0),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = y'_\\text{new} \\cdot \\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwith $y'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new},y_\\text{new})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=\\dfrac12,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac12 - 0 = \\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In our case,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =({x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into $y_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y$ and solve for the general formula for $y_\\text{new}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ (1-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is $x_\\text{new} = x + \\Delta x = 0 + \\dfrac12 = \\dfrac12.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{1/2}}{1-\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(\\sqrt{e}-2)}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y\\left(\\dfrac12\\right) = \\dfrac{4}{7} \\left(\\sqrt{e} - 2\\right).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221113 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56e30ebf-9265-5ba8-888d-6956206b542e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Two Steps Using the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/id #uuid "15820b47-eda7-55a7-9027-3a41831c71dc" :question/math-academy-id "e-21661" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny' = 4x^2 - y, \\qquad y(0)=0\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y\\left(\\dfrac12\\right)$ and $y(1).$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y_0 = y(x_0),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = y'_\\text{new} \\cdot \\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwith $y'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new},y_\\text{new})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(1).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=1$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{1-0}2 = \\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $\\Delta y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(4({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into $y_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y$ and solve for the general formula for $y_\\text{new}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2})}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y\\left(\\dfrac12\\right)$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx = 0,\\qquad y = 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\nx_\\text{new} = x + \\Delta x = 0 + \\dfrac12 = \\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2})}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(0+2{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2})}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac12, \\qquad y = \\dfrac13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\nx_\\text{new} = x + \\Delta x = \\dfrac12 + \\dfrac12 = 1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2})}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(\\frac{1}{3}+2\\cdot {1}^{2})}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny\\left(\\dfrac12\\right)\\approx\\dfrac{1}{3}, \\qquad\ny(1)\\approx\\dfrac{14}{9}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221862 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7095c46-33cf-5407-be83-70a49cf6eadd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a General Update Formula for the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd4410d-6096-5268-bc63-d77015ce9b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325994} {:answer/id #uuid "3d0d76d4-fdf0-5c58-8640-57094a8e0d3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325995} {:answer/id #uuid "d1c506b0-1af0-5d4f-9700-aed86aa76ce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325996} {:answer/id #uuid "c366c38a-ffcd-5bb4-b2a0-e080c13b9488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325997} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea4dcd4-044b-50bf-b26a-691a8ab0548e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c366c38a-ffcd-5bb4-b2a0-e080c13b9488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325997} :answer-field/id #uuid "23d59c99-8926-55b2-a5b5-70b2e7823ff4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "461042b3-69a6-56d4-910f-61f217280a46" :question/math-academy-id "q-325169" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={e}^{x}-3xy,\\,y(-2)=3\n$$\n\nThe **implicit** Euler method is applied with step size $Δx=1.$ \nFind the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and the current value $y.$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =({e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}) & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7095c46-33cf-5407-be83-70a49cf6eadd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a General Update Formula for the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8814e1d-cedb-5ab5-8535-05c4d45aff43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{\\text{new}}+{x}_{\\text{new}}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326001} {:answer/id #uuid "ddafc311-f418-5cdc-b862-2f594ea958c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{\\text{new}}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326002} {:answer/id #uuid "13d197e6-f8c4-5b3e-8f1b-00a396a179c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{3y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{3-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326003} {:answer/id #uuid "85b0a200-1b6e-5c66-93cc-955f97c43619" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{3y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{3+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326004} {:answer/id #uuid "7b77a2ad-405c-580b-a1b3-cdfecc7d228a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{3y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{3-3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13d197e6-f8c4-5b3e-8f1b-00a396a179c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{3y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{3-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326003} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa6ffff4-9879-50b4-9c71-2e681bccda98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02d633b4-d0e7-5727-8c57-6d89916e94a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-333415" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x+3xy,\\,y(-2)=-1\n$$\n\nThe **implicit** Euler method is applied with step size $Δx=\\frac{1}{3}.$ \nFind the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and the current value $y.$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(2{x}_{\\text{new}}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{\\text{new}}+{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{\\text{new}}+{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1-{x}_{\\text{new}}) & =y+\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ 3{y}_{\\text{new}}(1-{x}_{\\text{new}}) & =3y+2{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(3-3{x}_{\\text{new}}) & =3y+2{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{3y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{3-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7095c46-33cf-5407-be83-70a49cf6eadd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a General Update Formula for the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d3be92e-155c-5e65-97d2-407c37bb2364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326008} {:answer/id #uuid "432cc776-9925-5bb9-a7b1-bcea0a1e1b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-3y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326009} {:answer/id #uuid "0af547b3-23ee-5937-987a-bd196d265bd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326010} {:answer/id #uuid "8d1dce6f-e534-5ab1-9bcb-887c05e26b08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{1-3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326011} {:answer/id #uuid "4f9dac7a-139d-5cbf-adc5-2eaef1ef6f3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{1-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f9dac7a-139d-5cbf-adc5-2eaef1ef6f3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{1-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326012} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6a0fb07-3134-5d50-b6a9-925e19b51712" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5cc11f9d-82da-5dac-84c7-cca1eb3fc1cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-333421" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x-{x}^{2}+3xy,\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nThe **implicit** Euler method is applied with step size $Δx=1.$ \nFind the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and the current value $y.$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(2{x}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2{x}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1-3{x}_{\\text{new}}) & =y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{1-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7095c46-33cf-5407-be83-70a49cf6eadd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a General Update Formula for the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc321a2d-0eed-559d-ab24-e279cb2c6f05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{5y+4{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{5-5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326015} {:answer/id #uuid "090c9f28-41b1-5e05-a4bd-65ea9e0b1f1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326016} {:answer/id #uuid "74b48867-4d20-5f72-9ddd-c038a6eb8396" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{5y+4{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{5+5y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326017} {:answer/id #uuid "d362d310-b87f-5547-bf91-4472d5f8596e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{5y+4{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{5+5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326018} {:answer/id #uuid "c4442265-2300-5935-b841-07951fb9b637" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d362d310-b87f-5547-bf91-4472d5f8596e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{5y+4{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{5+5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326018} :answer-field/id #uuid "140f1fdf-81d1-57aa-bb5f-3d078050dcef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec64d979-a2b7-5216-964e-636ae65433ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-333423" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4{x}^{2}-5{x}^{2}y,\\,y(1)=0\n$$\n\nThe **implicit** Euler method is applied with step size $Δx=\\frac{1}{5}.$ \nFind the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and the current value $y.$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(4{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}) & =y+\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\ 5{y}_{\\text{new}}(1+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}) & =5y+4{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(5+5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}) & =5y+4{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{5y+4{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{5+5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7095c46-33cf-5407-be83-70a49cf6eadd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a General Update Formula for the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af85895f-3f7b-58b0-bb02-f83d43f74206" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+\\frac{1}{5}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326022} {:answer/id #uuid "5d1bf9d5-ab31-5340-9d22-ff956b5b3e2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{4+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326023} {:answer/id #uuid "005b85cc-79ba-53e8-af18-11cabf0825b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{4-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326024} {:answer/id #uuid "8d9d12f1-7ff6-50ff-a6d6-a6fe67cefbac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+\\frac{1}{5}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)y+\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326025} {:answer/id #uuid "7a46e7cd-ba54-5b20-8219-ce238f1cf37a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{4-{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "005b85cc-79ba-53e8-af18-11cabf0825b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{4-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326024} :answer-field/id #uuid "f543f8ce-c6c5-5c9e-aa3d-d45fd66009a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9c85170-a4b1-51b4-9704-03d5246a1950" :question/math-academy-id "q-333648" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=({x}^{2}+1)y+2x,\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nThe **implicit** Euler method is applied with step size $Δx=\\frac{1}{5}.$ \nFind the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and the current value $y.$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+2{x}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{1}{5}{y}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{5}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{1}{5}{y}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{5}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{5}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1-\\frac{1}{5}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-\\frac{1}{5}) & =y+\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ 5{y}_{\\text{new}}(\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}) & =5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(4-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}) & =5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{4-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "246a84b2-e9fa-58e5-858c-66c09e1c3bc0" :knowledge-point/title "Computing One Step Using the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fa4d7ed-4840-53c3-9f3b-dbedae036c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220660} {:answer/id #uuid "98b28495-b329-5133-9e43-f0e31e1b45f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.67" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220661} {:answer/id #uuid "b3bf3053-254a-5490-a405-c46ad1bbf1b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220662} {:answer/id #uuid "0a0a5bf1-d8bc-5a98-880c-6ebb9eca48bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98b28495-b329-5133-9e43-f0e31e1b45f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.67" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220661} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f64674-a074-545f-ae11-3a5489b803b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d1db9f63-1290-512d-8842-531c9d1381d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-339635" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y({x}^{2}+1),\\,y(-1)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with one step to approximate $y(-\\frac{1}{2})$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(-\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=-\\frac{1}{2}-(-1)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}\\cdot (({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1) & =y \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y}{1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-1+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y}{1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{1-{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & ≈2.67,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(-\\frac{1}{2})≈2.67.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56e30ebf-9265-5ba8-888d-6956206b542e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Two Steps Using the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87c25102-ce0c-52e0-934f-8de286bbfc72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220665} {:answer/id #uuid "d30a66e7-2803-5b83-9f5d-1afcec38ac94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220666} {:answer/id #uuid "72765ae4-8730-521e-8185-5dfe1480f1fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d30a66e7-2803-5b83-9f5d-1afcec38ac94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220666} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d8513dd-86c1-55a6-8535-19a4db6a6fee" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "941cc18f-4018-5d09-8407-5c63caf0caaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.67" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220669} {:answer/id #uuid "f1760199-0155-5137-a9ca-5f140e09a9e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220670} {:answer/id #uuid "1fffe1bc-17c3-5d4b-a826-889f17568aa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fffe1bc-17c3-5d4b-a826-889f17568aa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220671} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff32fbc2-b5bf-5c46-aa44-75c9b6eda67c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20432103-aae2-58eb-a669-f0d5cfc82ca5" :question/math-academy-id "q-339642" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x-3y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,y(1)≈$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(1).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=1$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-0}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(2{x}_{\\text{new}}-3{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+{x}_{\\text{new}})}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+{x}_{\\text{new}})}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1+\\frac{1}{2})}{5} \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=0.6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+{x}_{\\text{new}})}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(0.6+1)}{5} \\\\  & =0.64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(\\frac{1}{2})≈0.60,\\,y(1)≈0.64.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "246a84b2-e9fa-58e5-858c-66c09e1c3bc0" :knowledge-point/title "Computing One Step Using the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d50a28f9-cb8f-56b3-a1f9-1056ca545f34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326029} {:answer/id #uuid "a6dfc6d1-904a-5609-b822-4e79c4c46b38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326030} {:answer/id #uuid "a9482fcf-7fdd-535d-be01-fa12386d052b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.01" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326031} {:answer/id #uuid "2d3833d5-3283-5935-a734-f45b4ae49193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.71" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d50a28f9-cb8f-56b3-a1f9-1056ca545f34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326029} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6a75e46-943f-5a9b-9e6d-4d9b80905b8b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f75dcc74-76ed-50af-9566-63f6f6a83994" :question/math-academy-id "q-339691" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y-4x,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with one step to approximate $y(2)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(2)≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-0=2.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-4{x}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-8{x}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-8{x}_{\\text{new}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-8{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ (1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-8{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y-8{x}_{\\text{new}}}{1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+2=2.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y-8{x}_{\\text{new}}}{1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-8\\cdot 2}{1-2\\cdot {2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{7} \\\\  & ≈2.14,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈2.14.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326033 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "246a84b2-e9fa-58e5-858c-66c09e1c3bc0" :knowledge-point/title "Computing One Step Using the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "859fc32b-4b98-5422-9c06-481f0617aeb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326035} {:answer/id #uuid "3bdbfa2e-627e-5ca6-b759-2bb47921f7fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.99" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326036} {:answer/id #uuid "0e039f09-3ee9-56cc-b63a-bad1e888a9df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326037} {:answer/id #uuid "76b69cff-d903-5eab-9dd2-fa3855878889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76b69cff-d903-5eab-9dd2-fa3855878889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326038} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e475f53-b413-59a6-b2b1-cf341693d5bb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3dd9c8e3-0a5f-5518-8268-fe808abca826" :question/math-academy-id "q-339695" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y(2{e}^{x}+1),\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with one step to approximate $y(1)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(1)≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}\\cdot (2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}(2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{y}_{\\text{new}}(2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+1),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-{y}_{\\text{new}}(2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+1) & =y \\\\ (1-(2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+1)){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y}{1-(2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+1)} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =-\\frac{y}{2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =-\\frac{y}{2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2e} \\\\  & ≈-0.18,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈-0.18.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326039 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "246a84b2-e9fa-58e5-858c-66c09e1c3bc0" :knowledge-point/title "Computing One Step Using the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ca38e60-6b45-5e65-8da7-9dcae8d7417b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326041} {:answer/id #uuid "15be0de3-a3a7-541e-9f80-88d1acad2188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326042} {:answer/id #uuid "a3100e1e-1b4d-5ee4-bfff-3219b3e862cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326043} {:answer/id #uuid "6f224b64-f2da-5af3-8c01-5930b5b9ca1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15be0de3-a3a7-541e-9f80-88d1acad2188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326042} :answer-field/id #uuid "2032e6b7-15c6-5a51-9c0a-d0f3e7e39672" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72f212ba-86d7-561e-adb0-0049c49bcba3" :question/math-academy-id "q-339696" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y(4{e}^{x}-2),\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with one step to approximate $y(1)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(1)≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}\\cdot (4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-2)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}(4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{y}_{\\text{new}}(4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-2),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-{y}_{\\text{new}}(4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-2) & =y \\\\ (1-(4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-2)){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y}{1-(4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-2)} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y}{3-4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y}{3-4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3-4{e}^{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3-4e} \\\\  & ≈-0.25,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈-0.25.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326045 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "246a84b2-e9fa-58e5-858c-66c09e1c3bc0" :knowledge-point/title "Computing One Step Using the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "254ba5f6-99ea-56f3-a6c5-f29d2bd44bef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326047} {:answer/id #uuid "a590094d-1cdd-5c06-b85d-887b70c5bde8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326048} {:answer/id #uuid "dc892c02-c529-5b7d-96e9-a28df2c1696d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.05" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326049} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd20ef0-88a6-5798-9838-9bc8abf99156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dd20ef0-88a6-5798-9838-9bc8abf99156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326050} :answer-field/id #uuid "37a8f92c-c9d7-5da7-96c2-ebca0b24fccd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "117900e5-d11d-58f8-b65f-140bbdd217d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-339698" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=({x}^{2}+2)y+{e}^{x},\\,y(1)=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with one step to approximate $y(2)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(2)≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-1=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =((({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2){y}_{\\text{new}}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2){y}_{\\text{new}}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2){y}_{\\text{new}}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ (1-(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2)){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1-(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2)} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =-\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =-\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}+{e}^{2}}{1+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}+{e}^{2}}{5} \\\\  & ≈-1.58,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈-1.58.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326051 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56e30ebf-9265-5ba8-888d-6956206b542e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Two Steps Using the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7e75089-0d73-5b3e-bf31-5122bfadcecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326053} {:answer/id #uuid "a8bbc796-9cb2-5c5f-930a-feaf2befcff4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326054} {:answer/id #uuid "e394f15f-188f-5b12-916a-240a7a94dff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8bbc796-9cb2-5c5f-930a-feaf2befcff4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326054} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a9ff7a3-69ab-5583-a2f7-cce9862de625" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326052} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "def0ac28-809a-55c1-b573-08633d6e1560" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326057} {:answer/id #uuid "4c97e05d-0d0b-5310-8c8d-716e50359af1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326058} {:answer/id #uuid "d10bedc6-5e19-5d83-8d29-b481f61c22f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c97e05d-0d0b-5310-8c8d-716e50359af1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326058} :answer-field/id #uuid "489bd6e7-d489-5177-9a72-d4be5ff94ba3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "014d3463-d63f-5c65-a554-dfe15b02a633" :question/math-academy-id "q-339713" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-x-3y,\\,y(-1)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(-\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(0)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(-\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,y(0)≈$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(-1)$ and asked to find $y(0).$ The distance from $x=-1$ to $x=0$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{0-(-1)}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-{x}_{\\text{new}}-3{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y-{x}_{\\text{new}}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(-\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(0).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-1+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y-{x}_{\\text{new}}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1-(-\\frac{1}{2})}{5} \\\\  & =0.50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=0.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=0.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2\\cdot y-{x}_{\\text{new}}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0.5-0}{5} \\\\  & =0.20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(-\\frac{1}{2})≈0.50,\\,y(0)≈0.20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326060 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56e30ebf-9265-5ba8-888d-6956206b542e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Two Steps Using the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "832ec1df-cf30-5e90-b68c-7ad3e8eb253d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326062} {:answer/id #uuid "74c12d69-14f3-54a3-98c2-ce099fc1b29a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.67" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326063} {:answer/id #uuid "81ad7101-0c1b-52af-a337-bcfcd6bef27e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.00" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "832ec1df-cf30-5e90-b68c-7ad3e8eb253d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326062} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b7da530-e5be-5af4-8b91-6b697cd3bda7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34a8de28-e521-5e32-adb7-fe650e9969c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.67" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326066} {:answer/id #uuid "fc7858e2-6996-5fa0-a0a3-bbcc71adede3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326067} {:answer/id #uuid "6d2538f6-dcd1-5c6a-8255-b7b3bf0ce31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.00" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d2538f6-dcd1-5c6a-8255-b7b3bf0ce31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.00" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326068} :answer-field/id #uuid "f48b26b1-1c64-562b-ae38-3c05070930c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8baedbb2-ab4c-580d-acaf-08d946efa9a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-339717" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3x+y,\\,y(-1)=2\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(-\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(0)$  rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(-\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,y(0)≈$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(-1)$ and asked to find $y(0).$ The distance from $x=-1$ to $x=0$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{0-(-1)}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-3{x}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y-3{x}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(-\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(0).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,y=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-1+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y-3{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =5.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=5.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=0.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y-3{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5.5-3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(-\\frac{1}{2})≈5.50,\\,y(0)≈11.00.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326069 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56e30ebf-9265-5ba8-888d-6956206b542e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Two Steps Using the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e102d97e-ad41-5e05-9f03-67896a5930ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326071} {:answer/id #uuid "c1b91a3d-e960-5ed1-97e9-5ebe2acb0307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326072} {:answer/id #uuid "23ab9d4f-3ad5-5b22-8761-1f5fcb40b471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1b91a3d-e960-5ed1-97e9-5ebe2acb0307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326072} :answer-field/id #uuid "b93524ca-c3a0-5702-a487-5b79800baab9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326070} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30bc1266-281b-560a-901c-23c4ff4406be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326075} {:answer/id #uuid "a63f8e96-03af-5828-880b-623ddbc76c7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326076} {:answer/id #uuid "8c239742-99c5-5549-8bc7-eee961f5b6e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30bc1266-281b-560a-901c-23c4ff4406be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326075} :answer-field/id #uuid "a69ffcba-ac19-5039-bc40-9e55ea4b81cf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d535d60e-4068-5729-99a4-38ae3581a9c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-339719" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{2}y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$$\\,y(\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,y(1)≈$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(1).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=1$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-0}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ (1+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(2y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)}{1+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1}{2+2{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=1.3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1.3+{1}^{2}+1}{2+2({1}^{2})} \\\\  & =1.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(\\frac{1}{2})≈1.30,\\,y(1)≈1.15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56e30ebf-9265-5ba8-888d-6956206b542e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Two Steps Using the Implicit Euler Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c750f542-1d15-5a98-851e-3157a8a07c5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326080} {:answer/id #uuid "751ed622-c5b5-5ef5-96d8-50ec69c70cd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326081} {:answer/id #uuid "ef628596-caeb-53ec-a5fa-875de436d987" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "751ed622-c5b5-5ef5-96d8-50ec69c70cd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326081} :answer-field/id #uuid "8337ebdb-7432-534c-aba8-1a8f1e5c3a48" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc7569df-46eb-56bd-be3d-e8ca00b0523a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326084} {:answer/id #uuid "2896d3f8-fae6-5772-891c-23c8db39be68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326085} {:answer/id #uuid "fae59ae0-54e9-594f-8cd8-c7c6443fcc05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc7569df-46eb-56bd-be3d-e8ca00b0523a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326084} :answer-field/id #uuid "6407a46a-12bc-51b5-b3cd-9d0308928f3f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7d1b30e-1b06-58e8-b5bd-fe8664e41f56" :question/math-academy-id "q-339720" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=1-{x}^{2}+3{x}^{2}y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,y(1)≈$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(1).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=1$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-0}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+3({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2})+\\frac{3}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2})+\\frac{3}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ (1-\\frac{3}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}) \\\\ 2(1-\\frac{3}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y+(1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2-3({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2-3({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1)-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1}{2-3{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =2.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=2.2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2-3({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2.2-{1}^{2}+1}{2-3\\cdot {1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-4.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(\\frac{1}{2})≈2.20,\\,y(1)≈-4.40.\n$$"}]}
